description:
FILED s514d (Opus, 2026-10-10) while measuring #2590 on t/op/tiehandle.t (its `package Bar::Say; use base qw(Implement)` block aborts: rows 37-44 of the file never run).

A `package X;` switch inside a bare BLOCK that also holds a `local` is lowered by the nested-switch path (Parser2 _lower_block_1, the #3120 site), which emits at RUN TIME `(p-defclass X::plc-x () ())` -- a class with NO parents.  p-defclass compares parents, so it REDEFINES the class that `use base` had already given its parents: perl's `package X;` never changes @ISA.  The `use base` push also emits an unqualified `(p-push @ISA ...)` inside the block.

Minimal reproducer (perl 5.40.3 prints `hi [Implement] []`; PCL dies "Can't locate object method "hi" via package "Bar""):

    package Implement; sub hi { "hi" }
    package main;
    { package Bar; use base qw(Implement); local $\ = ""; print Bar->hi, " [@Bar::ISA] [@main::ISA]\n"; }

Without the `local` the same block works (it takes the section path).  Fix direction: a run-time package switch ensures the class EXISTS and never sets its parents (e.g. a p-defclass form that creates when absent and leaves an existing class alone); probe the `@ISA` push's package too.  Costs t/op/tiehandle.t rows 37-44.
